; expect 42
; Struct construction lays the fields out as consecutive words, so
; field i is readable as word i through `__load64` - the raw route,
; distinct from `540-field-access.ax`, which reads the same words
; through `p.x`.
;
; The `cast` is load-bearing and was not here originally. `__load64`
; is declared `Int -> Int -> Int` (axiom_sema::PRIMITIVES: every
; primitive is `Int`-typed, because primitives are where the type
; system stops), and a struct handle's type is `P`. Passing `p`
; directly is a type error that stage0 has always reported and stage1
; used to compile in silence, because stage1 had no type checker; the
; case passed by not being checked. `cast` reinterprets the machine
; word without converting it, which is exactly the handle-to-address
; move this test wants to make.
(struct P (x : Int) (y : Int))
(:: main Int)
(fn (main)
  (let ((p (P 40 2)))
    (+ (__load64 (cast Int p) 0) (__load64 (cast Int p) 1))))
